ur transmembrane spans, with cytosolic amino- and carboxy-termini. DMP1 is a membrane protein that may be involved in membrane fission during breakdown of the ER and the tonoplast during leaf senescence and in membrane fusion during vacuole biogenesis in roots [[cite:PUB00086645]]. Several DMP proteins are expressed in senescing organs (DMP1, -3, -4) or tissues that will stall later in development (DMP1, -2, -4, -7). These expression patterns strongly suggest involvement of several DMPs in various programmed cell death processes, e.g. senescence, dehiscence and abscission [[cite:PUB00136742]]. AtDMP8 and AtDMP9 however, have been shown to facilitate gamete fusion during double fertilisation in flowering plants [[cite:PUB00093467]].","domain_architectures":52,"interpro_id":"IPR007770","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":4715,"name":"Protein of unknown function (DUF679)","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF05078","proteins":4584,"proteomes":395,"short_name":"DUF679","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF05078","structures":0,"taxa":1097,"unknown_status":"UNKNOWN_CANDIDATE"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-08","members":"pfam-uniprot-uniref90-2026-10-07","worklist":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-08"},"members":[],"metadata":{"curation_status":"SEEDED","local_source":"source/data/families/PF05078.yaml","record":{"characterization_status":"UNSCORED","counters":{"alphafold_models":3757,"domain_architectures":52,"matches":4715,"proteins":4584,"proteomes":395,"structures":0,"taxa":1097},"curation_status":"SEEDED","description":"This family includes members such as plant proteins AtDMPs 1-10 (Arabidopsis thaliana DUF679 domain membrane proteins 1 -10) [[cite:PUB00136742]]. The AtDMP proteins are predicted to have four transmembrane spans, with cytosolic amino- and carboxy-termini. DMP1 is a membrane protein that may be involved in membrane fission during breakdown of the ER and the tonoplast during leaf senescence and in membrane fusion during vacuole biogenesis in roots [[cite:PUB00086645]]. Several DMP proteins are expressed in senescing organs (DMP1, -3, -4) or tissues that will stall later in development (DMP1, -2, -4, -7). These expression patterns strongly suggest involvement of several DMPs in various programmed cell death processes, e.g. senescence, dehiscence and abscission [[cite:PUB00136742]]. AtDMP8 and AtDMP9 however, have been shown to facilitate gamete fusion during double fertilisation in flowering plants [[cite:PUB00093467]].","id":"Pfam:PF05078","interpro_id":"InterPro:IPR007770","name":"Protein of unknown function (DUF679)","pfam_id":"PF05078","provenance":{"generated_at":"2026-10-08T02:48:09.822970Z","path":"data/worklists/interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-08.json","sha256":"9f0992961c30c5d92343a92aab000cd20b6c4213952b4c68408c3065779a46ec","snapshot_id":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-08","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/"},"seed_status":"UNKNOWN_CANDIDATE","short_name":"DUF679","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF05078"},"source":{"commit":"5f0bce3d349539563b98ebefd553d8d6be83e9b4","path":"data/families/PF05078.yaml","repository":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech","sha256":"bd464fefea6489a339d49ec66318df9c51ae740e5d9508d02213376266c1cede"}}}
